                        ],
                        "form": "most fleshly"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "90f5cca0-7fdd-3dc4-8bd7-116156989203",
                        "entry_id": "40eb6458-cd97-3b6d-975b-919611da7b66",
                        "glosses": [
                            "In a sensual way; in a sexual way; carnally."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "archaic"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9fa3fce3-9475-442e-908e-c017b460d1c1",
                                "sense_id": "90f5cca0-7fdd-3dc4-8bd7-116156989203",
                                "text": "Syr said Launcelot ye saye that that good knyȝt is my sone That ouȝtest thow to knowe and no man better said the good man / For thow knewest the doughter of kyng Pelles flesshely / and on her thow begattest Galahad / And that was he that at the feest of Pentecost satte in the sege peryllous"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1a38ed0e-905b-4104-9be8-4728557654f8",
                                "sense_id": "90f5cca0-7fdd-3dc4-8bd7-116156989203",
                                "text": "And the drunkard is with drink. And the ploughman is with his oxen. And the inhabitant of Ulverton doth loll fleshly abed."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
